# Custom Scrollbar Shells

<rule>
name: custom_scrollbar_shells
description: Use dedicated data-custom-scrollbar shells for scrollable panel content. Do not combine form-section-scroll with custom-scrollbar on the same element.

## Problem

`customScrollbar.js` auto-inits both `[data-custom-scrollbar]` elements and `.form-section-scroll:not([data-custom-scrollbar])`. Putting `form-section-scroll` on the same node as `data-custom-scrollbar`, or nesting both patterns, causes **double padding** and inconsistent scroll gutters (see config editor tree/checkpoints fix).

## Required pattern

Use a flex column shell with an inner scrollable wrapper created by `customScrollbar`:

```html
<div class="my-panel-body">
    <div class="my-scroll-shell scrollbar-padding" data-custom-scrollbar
        data-scrollable-wrapper-class="my-scrollable">
        <div class="my-scroll-inner">
            <!-- content -->
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
```

CSS (panel body holds flex/min-height; shell hides overflow; scrollable gets padding):

```css
#myModal .my-panel-body {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
}

#myModal .my-scroll-shell {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
}

#myModal .my-scrollable {
    height: 100%;
    overflow: auto;
    padding: 2px 4px 4px 0;
}
```

## Do not

- Add `form-section-scroll` to elements that already use `data-custom-scrollbar`
- Add `form-section-scroll` to the shell or inner wrapper when the shell owns scrolling
- Call `customScrollbar.forceReinit` on `.form-section-scroll` parents instead of the `[data-custom-scrollbar]` shell

## Reference implementations

- Config editor tree: `.config-editor-tree-scroll-shell` in `public/app.html` + `public/css/config-editor.css`
- Config editor values: `.config-editor-values-scroll-shell`
- Config editor checkpoints: `.config-editor-checkpoints-scroll-shell`
- Reinit after dynamic content: `configEditorApplet.reinitScrollbars()` → `forceReinit(shell)`

## After dialog/modal HTML changes

Wire reinit in `setTimeout(..., 0)` or post-`openModal` (same as config editor value/checkpoints modals).
</rule>
